cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or manuscript, please cite it as below."
title: "Same-Label Partner Averaging Inflates Unpaired Multi-Omics Fusion Estimates: A Pairing-Arithmetic Audit Applied to Alzheimer's Disease"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dutta"
    given-names: "Pijush Kanti"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "GITHUB_REPO_URL, to be inserted by author"
keywords:
  - multi-omics data integration
  - unpaired data
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - value of information
  - model calibration
  - reproducibility
abstract: >
  Reproducible code and results for a three-check audit of same-label partner
  averaging, the standard convention for estimating what a second molecular
  layer adds when no cohort has both layers measured on the same patients.
  Provides a pairing-arithmetic inflation identity, a combination-rule-free
  attainability bound, and a single-partner re-simulation with a significance
  test, applied to an open-access Alzheimer's disease case study built
  entirely on public GEO/Zenodo data with no controlled-access data use
  agreement required. Includes bootstrap-ensembled Stage-1 (mRNA) and Stage-2
  (methylation) classifiers, the pairing-arithmetic and attainability-bound
  checks, a single-partner (k=1) re-simulation, expanded external validation
  across three independent cohorts, cross-platform harmonization checks, and
  a leave-one-series-out retrain.
